You could encode a message entirely in who’s connected to whom. Keep every point on both strands fixed. Read the rungs two at a time. Straight means 0, crossed means 1. So straight · crossed · crossed · straight reads 0110. The strands supply the addresses. The connections carry the message.

The Pantheon version gets more interesting. Put original expressions on one strand and their possible meanings in another context on the other. Now the wiring is a translation key. A slow blink can connect to I remember in one wiring and take a beat in another. Same gesture. Same vocabulary. A different connection changes what the reader takes from it.

And here’s the wink. If we already share the original wiring, I can send you just the one change. One swapped pair of rungs can say which part of the old story to read differently.